  "notes": [
    "two levels below the lobby, in the Atrium Tower: the Grand Hall under the Centennial Ballroom, Hanover Hall to the south-east, the Chicago rooms west of the atrium elevators",
    "Grand Hall West and East are the exhibit halls, drawn as open floor: the venues file has no room for them. Grand Hall A to D are part of the East hall's floor, partitioned off along its north wall, which is why they are drawn inside its outline: Dragon Con's map calls C and D Grand Hall East C / D",
    "the Concourse is the pre-function area, 136 x 50 in the table, where Dragon Con's map marks its stage",
    "Hanover C, D and E are drawn from the wall they share on the Hanover corridor; the table makes E 5 ft wider than C and D"
  ]
